## Firmware (bundled default)

`firmware/boot.bin` — prebuilt nto-tests test firmware
(sha256 `5ec15e9a98a4adac2145386b4dc65204ada62b4123360c236be5aa80569b9b6e`,
3155332 bytes), built from:

| Component | Source | Revision |
|---|---|---|
| nto-tests | github.com/buncram/nto-tests | b2ef9e100f000725af4b9fe3aa94b610c370f6ba |
| xous-core (build sibling) | github.com/betrusted-io/xous-core | 53d772438a9aeea88972b59b9707a88142b63548 |
| rust | rustup, minimal | 1.90.0, target riscv32imac-unknown-none-elf |
| xpack riscv-none-elf-gcc | xpack-dev-tools | 15.2.0-1 |

Rebuild recipe (see README "Firmware"):

```
cargo xtask boot-image --no-default-features \
    --feature fast-fclk --feature quirks-pll --feature aes-zkn \
    --feature bio-mul --feature reset-value-tests --feature bio-tests
python3 ./merge_cm7.py --rv32=rv32.bin --cm7=cm7/mbox.bin --out-file=boot.bin
```

`cm7/mbox.bin` is checked into nto-tests (no arm toolchain needed). The
bundled image additionally carries a one-line sim early-quit hook in
`tests/src/main.rs` (drives `finisher.v`'s quit input so the run ends at
`$finish`); rebuilds without it simply run until `VEXSIM_TIMEOUT`.

## Source patches (applied at container start; the submodule checkout stays
## pristine except deps/migen/migen/fhdl/tracer.py, which is patched in place,
## so `git -C baochip-1x status` there shows that one file as modified)

- `patches/migen-tracer-py312.py` — upstream migen fix for Python 3.11+
  bytecode tracing (`get_var_name` must skip CACHE/EXTENDED_ARG opcodes and
  index STORE_DEREF against `co_nlocals`). Without it, Litex CSR auto-naming
  dies on py3.12 with "Cannot extract CSR name from code".
- `patches/veril-fst-close.cpp` — replacement for the Litex sim-core
  `veril.cpp`: registers `litex_sim_tracer_close()` with `atexit` +
  SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP so the FST/VCD writer emits its header, hierarchy,
  geometry and seek tables (upstream never calls `Writer::close()`, leaving
  traces that no reader can open after `$finish` or a timeout kill).
- `patches/daric-svd-aoram-region.patch` — manual patch for firmware
  rebuilds only: adds the AORAM memory region (0x50300000, 16 KiB; mirrors
  `bao1x_peri.svd` in xous-core) to `baochip-1x/deps/nto-tests/svd/daric.svd`.
  utralib's `build.rs` regenerates `generated.rs` from the SVDs on every
  fresh checkout; the shipped SVDs omit AORAM, but `bao1x-hal` references
  `utralib::HW_AORAM_MEM`. With the patch, generated output is byte-identical
  to the native build's stale `generated.rs` (verified via md5).

